# A module's file can declare top-level constants its functions read
# (kexhq/kex#559, as the AI review on #566 pointed out). The dependency merge
# dropped every main block wholesale, and a top-level `let` parses into one,
# so `Tariff.total` failed to check with "Undefined identifier: rate".
using Tariff

main do
  IO.printLine(total(2))
  IO.printLine(Tariff.total(5))
end
